    "text": "<p>A current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> flows for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> through an electrolytic cell containing a molten salt of metal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>. This results in the decomposition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of metal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> at the cathode. The oxidation&nbsp;state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> in the molten salt is:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
